    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Churches Estate Agents are delighted to present No. 4 Coundon Court, a substantial detached bungalow lovingly maintained offering a sun-drenched South facing garden and tranquil living tucked away in one of Killiney’s most coveted tree lined cul-de-sacs.\r\n\r\nApproaching the property, an expansive tarmac and gravel driveway provides ample parking for multiple vehicles. Meticulously sculpted topiary, mature planting beds and manicured hedging wrap the front grounds complemented by gated side access on both flanks.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises of a bright central entrance hall that sets a grand tone upon entry. At the rear of the foyer a pleasant sun room with access to the surrounding garden. To the rear lies an expansive, light-filled formal living room complete with an open fireplace, double aspect windows and sliding patio doors opening to the surrounding gardens and seating area. \r\n\r\nThe heart of the home is an impressive open-plan kitchen and family dining space featuring fully integrated cabinetry, extensive counter space and an island unit. This seamlessly transitions into a bright dining area and cosy family nook with a feature stove and sliding glass doors leading straight onto the sunny paved terrace.\r\n\r\nBack through the inner hallway with skylights above leads into the sleeping wing of four generously proportioned bedrooms to front, all enjoying quiet views of the surrounding grounds alongside a well-appointed family bathroom. The primary is double aspect with its own ensuite, shower and built in wardrobes. \r\n\r\nSetting itself apart from the rest, this home is enveloped by a wonderfully private, south-facing garden that wraps around the entirety of the home. Deliberately landscaped to capture the sunshine from dawn until dusk, the grounds feature multiple sunny seating areas and terraces perfect for al fresco dining, lush planting beds with vibrant seasonal flora, a gravelled garden and mature trees providing complete seclusion. A greenhouse, large block-built storage shed and practical side access on both flanks complete this exceptionally rare outdoor space given its location.\r\n\r\nThe location of this property is superb, enjoying great ease of access to both Killiney and Dalkey’s growing number of popular amenities, including excellent shopping facilities, popular restaurants, pubs, boutiques, eateries and specialist delicatessens. Dalkey hosts a number of social events throughout the year including the renowned Lobster and Book Festivals. There is also an abundance of highly regarded schools both Primary and Secondary in the area. \r\n\r\nThe area also has numerous transport links including Killiney DART station, easy access to the M50/N11 road networks, Aircoach providing swift and direct access to the airport as well as numerous Dublin Bus routes all close at hand. \r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
